3. THE ONE CONDITION: PIN THE SOURCE LINK
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------

If you distribute the Software, a modified version, or a compiled build of it,
you must include and keep visible a link to the Original Source.

"Pinned" means the link must be:

  a) written out in full, pointing at the Original Source, with no URL
     shortener, redirect or intermediary;
  b) permanently placed where users of your distribution can see it;
  c) present in every place your project is published, for example the mod
     page, repository README, release notes, in-game or in-app about screen,
     or the description of your download.

The link must remain pinned for as long as your distribution is available.
Removing it, hiding it, or replacing it with a link to your own fork violates
this license.

The minimum acceptable attribution is the following line, kept intact:

  Based on Grape - https://github.com/okhx/grapebot

